        <span itemprop="subject">the inorganic particles 9</span>
        <span itemprop="definition">serve as a kind of spacer capable of maintaining the physical shape of the porous coating layer 3 .</span>
        <meta itemprop="num_attr" content="0059">
      </li>
      <li itemprop="definitions" itemscope repeat>
        <span itemprop="subject">the interstitial volume</span>
        <span itemprop="definition">refers to a space limited by substantially being in surface contact with the particles of the inorganic particles 9 and the particulate binder polymers 5 and 7 .</span>
        <meta itemprop="num_attr" content="0059">
      </li>
      <li itemprop="definitions" itemscope repeat>
        <span itemprop="subject">the separator 10</span>
        <span itemprop="definition">since the inorganic particles 9 generally have characteristics that do not change their physical properties even at a high temperature of 200° C. or higher, the separator 10 has excellent heat resistance by the porous organic/inorganic composite coating layer 3 .</span>
        <meta itemprop="num_attr" content="0059">
      </li>
      <li itemprop="definitions" itemscope repeat>
        <span itemprop="subject">the porous organic/inorganic composite coating layer 3</span>
        <span itemprop="definition">may have a thickness in a range of 1 to 50  ⁇ m, 2 to 30  ⁇ m, or 2 to 20  ⁇ m based on what is formed on either side of the porous substrate 1 .</span>
        <meta itemprop="num_attr" content="0059">
